.TH quicklisp-user-setup "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
quicklisp-user-setup \- Install Quicklisp into the current user's home
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quicklisp-user-setup
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B quicklisp-user-setup
installs Quicklisp for the current user by loading the system wide
.I /opt/quicklisp/lib/quicklisp.lisp
downloaded by
.BR quicklisp-setup (1)
and running the
.I quicklisp-user-setup.lisp
script from the SMI library directory with
.BR sbcl (1).
The result is a per user Quicklisp under
.IR ~/quicklisp/ ,
which Common Lisp scripts load to fetch and cache libraries, see
.BR hello-lisp (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/quicklisp/lib/quicklisp.lisp
System wide Quicklisp bootstrap, from
.BR quicklisp-setup (1).
.TP
.I $(smi-lib-location)/quicklisp-user-setup.lisp
The setup script.
.TP
.I ~/quicklisp/
The resulting per user installation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quicklisp-setup (1),
.BR sbcl (1),
.BR hello-lisp (1),
.BR smi-cl-test (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Imre Tabur <imre.tabur@mail.ee>
